From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cliff Brake <cbrake@bec-systems.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thin_archive: add symbol table when not using lld on linux

When using clang with GNU ld (not lld), the linker requires archives to
have a symbol table index. The thin_archive config was only adding the
symbol table (-s) for the !is_clang case (GCC), but GNU ld needs it
regardless of which compiler created the archive.

Without this fix, GNU ld fails with:
  error adding symbols: archive has no index; run ranlib to add one

Extend the condition to also include the is_clang && !use_lld case on
Linux, ensuring GNU ld always gets archives with a symbol table.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Cliff Brake <cbrake@bec-systems.com>
---
 chromium/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/chromium/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chromium/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -2516,7 +2516,8 @@ config("export_dynamic") {
 # 2. Remove the thin_archive config, so that the .a file actually contains all
 #    .o files, instead of just references to .o files in the build directoy
 config("thin_archive") {
-  if ((is_apple && use_lld) || (is_linux && !use_lld && !use_mold)) {
+  if ((is_apple && use_lld) || (is_linux && (!is_clang || !use_lld) && !use_mold)) {
+
     # The macOS and iOS linker ld64.ldd doesn't support thin archive without
     # symbol table, gcc on linux also throws the error `archive has no index`.
     arflags = [
